<!-- ===== SECTION 2: QUEUE & WAIT TIME ===== -->
<section id="queue-wait-analysis" class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">2</span>
    <h2>Queue Length &amp; Waiting Time Analysis</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-intro">Examining queue lengths and waiting times across station types, time slots, vehicle types, and traffic density to identify bottleneck patterns and their impact on customer experience.</p>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Average Wait Time Heatmap (minutes)</h3>
      <table class="heatmap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Off-Peak</th><th>Peak</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Highway</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">9.63</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">9.55</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Urban</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">9.54</td>
            <td class="heat-low">9.31</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout callout-insight" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <div class="callout-title">Analysis</div>
        Wait times are remarkably consistent across location types and time slots (range: 9.31&ndash;9.63 min). The variation is narrow (&lt;3.5%), suggesting the network is not experiencing severe localized bottlenecks but rather a systemic baseline wait time across all configurations.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Average Queue Length Heatmap (vehicles)</h3>
      <table class="heatmap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Off-Peak</th><th>Peak</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Highway</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">4.70</td>
            <td class="heat-low">4.47</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Urban</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">4.60</td>
            <td class="heat-mid">4.52</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout callout-insight" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <div class="callout-title">Analysis</div>
        Queue lengths average 4.5&ndash;4.7 vehicles across all segments. Notably, off-peak queues are slightly longer than peak queues&mdash;a counterintuitive pattern that may indicate scheduling or capacity allocation is not aligned with actual arrival patterns.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Wait Time Distribution</h3>
      <div class="chart-container">
        <canvas id="chartWaitDist"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Wait Time by Vehicle Type</h3>
      <div class="chart-container">
