  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#e02424;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-high">High Priority</span> Implement Peak-to-Off-Peak Load Shifting</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> Peak station loads average 84.1 kW (2.4x off-peak), and the optimization reward drops from -7.1 (off-peak) to -19.8 (peak)&mdash;a 179% deterioration. Meanwhile, off-peak renewable penetration is 35% higher.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Introduce time-of-use pricing with meaningful differentials (current pricing shows near-zero demand correlation at r = -0.012). Offer 15&ndash;25% discounts during off-peak windows and 10&ndash;20% surcharges during peak periods. Target shifting 15&ndash;20% of peak sessions to off-peak.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> Reduced grid stress, improved optimization reward, higher renewable energy utilization, and more even charger utilization across the day.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#e02424;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-high">High Priority</span> Deploy Smart Charging &amp; Partial-Charge Options</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> All vehicle types charge to ~98.5% SOC, with average sessions consuming 39 kWh over 179 minutes. Full-charge behavior maximizes dwell time and reduces charger turnover.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Introduce an "80% quick charge" option that stops at 80% SOC. At typical charge curves, this could reduce session duration by 25&ndash;35% (the final 20% of SOC takes disproportionate time). Provide pricing incentives for partial charges during high-demand periods.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> 25&ndash;35% reduction in average session duration during peak, directly improving charger throughput and reducing queue wait times.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#c27803;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-medium">Medium Priority</span> Accelerate DC Fast Charger Deployment</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> 7 kW chargers (25% of sessions) have an average session time of 339 minutes (5.6 hours), compared to 48 minutes for 50 kW DC fast chargers&mdash;a 7x throughput difference. Energy delivered per session is equivalent across power levels.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Prioritize 50 kW DC fast charger installations at high-demand Urban stations (ST012, ST003, ST007, ST004). Consider upgrading existing 7 kW stalls at these locations. Target a charger mix weighted 40&ndash;50% toward 22+ kW.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> Doubling throughput at upgraded stations would effectively add capacity without building new stations, reducing average wait times and queues.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#c27803;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-medium">Medium Priority</span> Redesign Dynamic Pricing to Track Grid Signals</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> The current pricing mechanism has near-zero correlation with demand (r = -0.012) and renewable availability (r = -0.005). Pricing is effectively static and fails to incentivize grid-optimal behavior.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Implement real-time pricing that incorporates: (1) grid load level with tiered surcharges above 60 kW station load, (2) renewable availability bonus of 5&ndash;10% discount when renewable ratio exceeds 35%, and (3) queue-based pricing with a small premium when queue length exceeds 5 vehicles.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> Price-responsive demand would naturally distribute load toward low-stress, high-renewable periods, directly improving the three optimization reward drivers.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#0e9f6e;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-green">Sustainability</span> Launch "Green Charging Windows" Program</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> Renewable ratio varies from 29.0% (peak) to 39.3% (off-peak). The optimization reward is most strongly correlated with renewable ratio (r = +0.59), yet no mechanism currently incentivizes green charging.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Publish real-time "Green Score" at each station. Create a loyalty program that rewards off-peak and high-renewable sessions with credits or reduced rates. Market off-peak slots as premium sustainability choices to corporate fleet operators.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> Increasing the network-wide renewable ratio from 35.4% to 40%+ would significantly improve optimization rewards and sustainability metrics, while differentiating the network in a competitive market.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card" style="border-left-color:#0e9f6e;">
    <h4><span class="rec-tag tag-green">Operational</span> Address Off-Peak Queue Anomaly</h4>
    <p><strong>Problem:</strong> Queue lengths are slightly higher during off-peak (4.65) than peak (4.50), despite 62.5% of all sessions occurring off-peak. This counterintuitive pattern suggests charger capacity allocation may not match arrival distribution.</p>
    <p><strong>Action:</strong> Audit station-level charger availability during off-peak hours. Investigate whether chargers are being taken offline for maintenance during off-peak or if capacity is being reserved. Ensure at least the same number of active chargers are available during off-peak as peak periods.</p>
    <p><strong>Expected Impact:</strong> Resolving this anomaly could reduce off-peak wait times, which in turn makes off-peak slots more attractive for load-shifting programs.</p>
